# ecosyste.ms may be the hidden gem

This one is almost tailor-made for the factory.

ecosyste.ms exposes open APIs covering roughly:

* 14M+ packages across 100+ package sources;
* hundreds of millions of repositories;
* billions of public repository timeline events;
* hundreds of millions of commits;
* issues and pull requests;
* dependency graphs;
* Docker images;
* sponsors;
* Open Collective funding;
* Dependabot activity. ([Ecosystems][6])

Most endpoints are public and OpenAPI-described. ([Ecosystems][6])

They even maintain MCP-related projects themselves. ([GitHub][7])

This could let you measure things ordinary GitHub-star trackers can't:

```text
langgraph package installs
        ↓
repos depending on langgraph
        ↓
new dependencies/month
        ↓
commit activity
        ↓
issue activity
        ↓
maintainer activity
```

So instead of saying:

> LangGraph has lots of stars.

you might say:

```text
GitHub attention          +4%
Package downloads         +22%
New dependent repos       +31%
Active maintainers        stable
Issue creation            +19%
Research mentions         +15%
```

That's actual market intelligence.

