# Cloudflare Radar gives you global Internet attention

Cloudflare Radar has a **free API** exposing aggregated Internet usage from Cloudflare's network and its public DNS resolver. ([Cloudflare Docs][9])

It includes APIs for:

```text
top domains
trending domains
domain rank time series
technology trends
```

and ranking time series can be aggregated at intervals from minutes through months. ([Cloudflare Docs][10])

That's extremely interesting for:

```text
openai.com
anthropic.com
huggingface.co
openrouter.ai
cursor.com
langchain.com
```

You won't get exact user numbers.

But you can detect:

```text
relative traffic trajectory
domain-rank movements
interest spikes
regional changes
```

Think of it as:

```text
WEB_ATTENTION
```

rather than usage.

