# Google Trends finally has an API

Google launched an official Trends API in alpha.

It provides a rolling **five-year window**, daily/weekly/monthly/yearly aggregation, geographic breakdowns, and—importantly—consistent scaling across queries, making longitudinal comparison much more useful than the old UI. ([Google for Developers][11])

It's still limited-access alpha, however. ([Google for Developers][11])

Google also now exposes trend-related concepts through its Ads APIs, including classifications such as:

```text
EMERGING
RISING
SUSTAINED
DECLINING
```

and historical topic trend data. ([Google for Developers][12])

For your oracle:

```text
"Claude Code"
"MCP"
"AI agent"
"LangGraph"
"OpenRouter"
"local LLM"
```

could produce:

```text
search_interest
velocity
acceleration
regional_diffusion
related_queries
```

Useful—but I would rank Google Trends below actual package/inference usage.

