# Research velocity: OpenAlex

This should absolutely be in the market layer.

OpenAlex provides a structured research graph covering scholarly works, authors, institutions, topics, funders and related entities, with filtering, grouping and search APIs. ([OpenAlex][13])

Its basic API is free with a free API key, and the data itself is CC0. ([OpenAlex][14])

This lets you calculate:

```text
papers/month
authors/month
institutions entering topic
citation growth
topic acceleration
cross-topic movement
```

For example:

```text
MCP                    2025 → 2026 ↑↑
agent memory            ↑
agent architecture      ↑↑
LLM routing             ↑
self-evolving agents    ↑↑↑
```

Much stronger than just scraping arXiv search pages.

