# MCP itself gives you another ecosystem oracle

The official MCP Registry now exposes a standardized REST/OpenAPI registry for publicly available MCP servers. ([GitHub][15])

The registry is intended as the centralized public source of metadata and exposes standardized installation/configuration metadata. ([Model Context Protocol][16])

So poll it every few hours/daily and maintain:

```text
servers_total
new_servers/day
new_servers/category
new_publishers
new_versions
language/runtime
package type
transport
capability tags
```

Then you can say:

```text
database MCP servers       +18% MoM
browser MCP servers         +7%
developer tooling          +32%
finance MCP                ...
```

without relying on vibes.

Smithery also exposes a searchable MCP registry API containing fields including verification and `useCount`, which provides an additional adoption signal. ([Smithery][17])

Triangulate:

```text
Official MCP Registry presence
+
Smithery useCount
+
GitHub repo health
+
package installs
```

Now MCP market intelligence becomes surprisingly strong.

