# Developer adoption surveys are important calibration

The Stack Overflow Developer Survey is especially useful because it tells you whether telemetry proxies resemble human-reported usage.

The 2025 survey reported that 84% of respondents were using or planning to use AI tools, while 51% of professional developers reported daily AI-tool usage. ([Stack Overflow Developer Survey][18])

It also contains explicit sections on:

```text
AI models
AI agents
agent orchestration tools
agent observability/security
out-of-box assistants
```

including reported usage of orchestration frameworks. ([Stack Overflow Developer Survey][18])

Our World in Data republishes some of this as machine-readable downloadable/API-backed data, which is useful for historical series. ([Our World in Data][19])

This is your:

```text
SURVEY_ADOPTION
```

signal.

